  "firmwareSourceVersion": "Released image reports ESP-IDF v6.1-dirty; exact private build revision is not established. Public source comparison pinned to fff9895c82d744c7237be8847347bdd1b07c6643.",
  "semantics": {
    "controller": "Separate MSPI2(system)/MSPI3(peripheral) register maps. Header reset/masks. APB reset clears controller state but preserves external mode/backing. Successful synchronous commands raise raw slave/master end bits3/4; W1C clears. Enabled IRQ routing and MSPI2 raw events remain unsupported. ECC encoding/address conversion is rejected.",
    "device": "Caller supplies MR0,1,2,3,4,8 and independent backing size. No inferred identity,capacity,good-die flag or automatic allocation. AP datasheet section6.7: repeated read pairs4->MR4/MR8,8->MR8/MR0; mode write affects one addressed byte only. Writes to RO/undefined mode addresses reject.",
    "array": "Serial writes mutate the same array that reads and CPU MMU access use. X8/X16 addresses,wrap/hybrid bursts,linear reads and bounded row crossing follow sections6.1/6.2/table20. Bounds/phase checks occur before mutation. FIFO limits and unsupported DDR/address/CRC formats reject.",
    "gating": "Actual commands require APB/core clock,PHY,DQS,CS1,16-bit command/32-bit address and expected phases. Attached-device CPU reads/writes/fetches additionally require configured MSPI2 AXI and command formats. Isolated raw-MMU fixtures retain explicit backing without a serial device.",
    "timing": "Functional synchronous transfers,not analog calibration. DLL/drive/delay settings retain configuration; successful tuning reads reflect real stored data across these represented settings,not measured timing margin."
  },
  "fixture": {
    "path": "firmware/s31-uart-probe/psram-controller-probe.S",
    "runs": [
      "test external_s31_psram_serial_reads_writes_and_executes_with_device_power_clock_and_axi_negatives ... S31 PSRAM serial mode=0 steps=292 stop=Waiting commands=[2, 1, 1, 1] retired=1",
      "S31 PSRAM serial mode=1 steps=45 stop=Trap(Exception(7)) commands=[0, 0, 0, 0] retired=0",
      "S31 PSRAM serial mode=2 steps=40 stop=Trap(Exception(7)) commands=[0, 0, 0, 0] retired=0",
      "S31 PSRAM serial mode=3 steps=41 stop=Trap(Exception(7)) commands=[0, 0, 0, 0] retired=0",
      "S31 PSRAM serial mode=4 steps=49 stop=Trap(Exception(7)) commands=[0, 0, 0, 0] retired=0",
      "S31 PSRAM serial mode=5 steps=133 stop=Trap(Exception(1)) commands=[2, 1, 1, 1] retired=0",
      "S31 PSRAM serial mode=6 steps=135 stop=Trap(Exception(1)) commands=[2, 1, 1, 1] retired=0",
      "S31 PSRAM serial mode=7 steps=46 stop=Trap(Exception(7)) commands=[0, 0, 0, 0] retired=0",
      "S31 PSRAM serial mode=8 steps=47 stop=Trap(Exception(7)) commands=[0, 0, 0, 0] retired=0",
      "S31 PSRAM serial mode=9 steps=90 stop=Trap(Exception(7)) commands=[2, 1, 0, 0] retired=0"
    ],
    "positive": "Guest reads real mode pairs,writes MR8 while ignoring extra bus byte,writes two instructions via MSPI3,reads them back,configures MMU/MSPI2 AXI and fetches them from the same backing. Returns42,emitsPASS,retires memory entry once; command-class counters[2,1,1,1].",
    "negative": "Absent device/DQS/PHY/core clock,invalid MR/opcode and absent backing all fail actual commands. Closed AXI or removed DQS fail instruction fetch. No negative retires the memory entry or prints success."
  },
